          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "Peak position can indicate identity, while calibrated signal strength can help estimate concentration. Conditions still matter: temperature, excitation, instrument response, and overlapping signals can change what is observed. Spectroscopy is powerful because it connects a precise measurement to reference physics, not because every colored line explains itself."
